{
"dur": 48.12,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 6.28,
"text": "Nvidia had one lifeline: a contract with Sega to build the graphics chip for its next game console.",
"end": 6.555
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.555,
"vo_start": 6.83,
"vo_end": 12.625,
"text": "But that chip was based on the same curved-surface design, the one the rest of the industry was abandoning.",
"end": 12.9
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 12.9,
"vo_start": 13.175,
"vo_end": 19.071,
"text": "If they finished it, they'd spend a year building something dead. If they quit, they'd lose their only paying customer.",
"end": 19.346
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 19.346,
"vo_start": 19.621,
"vo_end": 29.821,
"text": "So Jensen flew to Japan and did something unusual. He told Sega's chief executive, Shoichiro Irimajiri, that Nvidia's approach was wrong, and that Sega should find another partner.",
"end": 30.096
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 30.096,
"vo_start": 30.371,
"vo_end": 36.41,
"text": "Then he asked for the rest of the money anyway. As an investment, not a payment, because without it Nvidia would go under.",
"end": 36.685
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 36.685,
"vo_start": 36.96,
"vo_end": 42.676,
"text": "Irimajiri agreed. Jensen has said the only reason was that Irimajiri liked him.",
"end": 42.951
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 42.951,
"vo_start": 43.226,
"vo_end": 47.17,
"text": "That five million dollars bought Nvidia about six months.",
"end": 48.12
}
],
